From 0e70c1f4b71bb3b4a0eeac97ca0b6e8b68197074 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:53:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(batch-02): implement the missing
 ClamAvScanner::scanStream and harden the upload scan lane

UploadScanService::scanRecord() calls $this->scanner->scanStream() on the
quarantine-disk branch - the path every scanned upload takes. The method was
declared on no interface and implemented by no class, so that branch died with
'Call to undefined method' and the malware gate never ran.

Declared on App\\Contracts\\Security\\MalwareScanner and implemented. It is the
only implementer in the repository, so the contract change is safe.

Nine further defects fixed in the same scanner:
  - reply read with fgets() against a protocol that NUL-terminates, so every
    scan stalled the full timeout before parsing anything
  - fwrite() return ignored: a short write scanned a truncated file and clamd
    answered 'stream: OK' for bytes it never saw
  - fread() === '' treated as EOF, truncating the stream the same way
  - FOUND checked after OK; detection is now parsed first
  - unix socket support promised by the docblock never existed
  - getVersionInfo() invented 'ClamAV 1.3' while claiming engine_active
  - exception message (host:port) interpolated into the persisted threat_name
  - no file-size ceiling
  - file_exists() rather than is_file()

Tests: 16 new (tests/Feature/Compliance/UploadClamAvScannerTest.php).
Pre-existing Stack B suites still green: ClamAvScannerTest 8/8,
AntimalwareUploadGateTest 6/6.

Audit and corrections reconciliation: docs/BATCH-02-AUDIT.md
